{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-069a5886-04eb-4f47-9b62-234f6f047ad0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2adf5d678e7929e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E001.md","content":"# RHCL official xKS support status and deployment mechanism validation\n\n## Description\n\nResolve the strategic dependency on RHCL (Red Hat Common Libraries) official support for non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS) environments. On RHOAI, RHCL deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) via OLM; on xKS (Helm-only installation), the official support status and deployment mechanism are unknown. This investigation confirms the RHCL team's commitment, timeline, and the concrete mechanism by which Kuadrant can be deployed on CKS, and selects the deployment path for all downstream MaaS xKS work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to confirm: official xKS support commitment, timeline, and ownership boundaries (Sprint 1 validation per the strategy).\n- Determine whether official RHCL Helm charts for Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on xKS exist or are planned, and their availability date for CKS.\n- Evaluate the strategy's priority-ordered deployment options and select the mechanism for CKS:\n  1. Primary: official RHCL Helm charts (requires OpenShift team commitment).\n  2. Fallback: standalone Authorino + Limitador deployed via upstream Helm charts.\n  3. Contingency: direct Envoy ext_authz integration bypassing Kuadrant.\n- Confirm compatibility constraints with the MaaS integration surface (Kuadrant AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy CRs generated by the MaaS controller) for each option.\n- If RHCL support is not committed, escalate to product leadership per the strategy and document the selected fallback mechanism and its long-term viability implications.\n- Deliverable: a decision record stating the selected deployment mechanism, the RHCL commitment status, and the implications for MaaS xKS (including whether the MaaS AuthPolicy/TokenRateLimitPolicy integration remains unchanged).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- RHCL official xKS support commitment status is confirmed in writing (committed / not committed, with timeline if committed).\n- A deployment mechanism for Kuadrant on CKS is selected and justified against the MaaS integration surface (AuthPolicy, TokenRateLimitPolicy CRs).\n- If RHCL is not committed: escalation to product leadership is triggered and the fallback mechanism (standalone Authorino + Limitador, or direct Envoy ext_authz) is selected with documented viability trade-offs.\n- The decision record identifies which downstream MaaS xKS work changes scope under the selected mechanism.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy).\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- The OpenShift RHCL team can be engaged within Sprint 1 (strategy: \"needs immediate validation with OpenShift team\").\n- Gateway API implementation on CKS (Istio service mesh on CoreWeave) is confirmed available and is not re-litigated here.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63769,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"9f9f67f1-b4dd-4803-9a5b-c00a1d19baba","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:31:51.776Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
