ation path (`auth.identity.groups`).\n- Confirm the API key authentication flow (`sk-oai-*` via the maas-api callback validation endpoint) is genuinely OIDC-agnostic and requires no changes.\n- Deliverable: a feasibility decision record covering (a) AuthPolicy OIDC reuse verdict with the exact change delta, and (b) groupClaimPath feasibility verdict (code change possible vs Tenant CRD frozen).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A concrete verdict on AuthPolicy external-OIDC reuse: configuration-only, or an enumerated list of required code changes in the MaaS components.\n- A concrete verdict on group claim path configurability: either the Tenant CRD change is feasible (with the freeze-policy confirmation from release management), or the fallback is confirmed necessary (document required claim format, push IdP configuration burden to customers).\n- The API key flow's OIDC independence is verified against the codebase with cited evidence.\n- Representative OIDC provider group claim formats are documented against the CEL predicate path.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (feasibility portion).\n- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) — feasibility portion.\n\n## Open Questions Resolved by this Investigation\n\n- \"Can we leverage existing MaaS AuthPolicy with external OIDC, or are changes needed?\"\n- \"How do we map external identities to MaaS subscriptions/tiers?\" (claim path feasibility portion)\n- Assumption: \"OIDC group claim path can be made configurable without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes — Needs validation.\"\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64632,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"df767bef-21d3-42d5-8607-9b300462