{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f5b7b03a-5a20-4ecb-ae3e-0188dd7a3a13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89fd8fe0f486f641","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E003.md","content":"# CKS observability infrastructure accessibility validation\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether the CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service) standard observability infrastructure — the Prometheus instance and Grafana Loki log aggregation — is accessible for MaaS metrics and logs. The strategy assumes both are available (CoreWeave standard infrastructure), but the assumption is explicitly marked \"Needs validation\". The answer determines whether the CKS observability integration is configuration-only or requires provisioning a dedicated stack for MaaS.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Confirm with the xKS Platform team and CoreWeave that the CKS Prometheus instance can scrape MaaS metrics endpoints (dedicated metrics listener) from the MaaS namespace, and identify any scrape-config or network-policy constraints.\n- Confirm that CKS Grafana Loki is accessible for structured JSON logs emitted by the MaaS components (maas-api, Authorino, Limitador), and identify the required label scheme and log shipping path.\n- Confirm whether Perses dashboards can be deployed and rendered against the CKS Prometheus instance for MaaS metrics.\n- Determine whether an OpenTelemetry collector is available on CKS for distributed tracing, or whether tracing export needs a dedicated endpoint.\n- Document any access constraints (authentication, tenancy, quotas) and the resulting integration approach.\n- Deliverable: a validation record stating, per infrastructure element (Prometheus, Loki, Perses, OTel collector), whether it is accessible as-is, accessible with configuration, or must be provisioned for MaaS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Prometheus scrape accessibility for MaaS metrics endpoints is confirmed or refuted with evidence from the CKS environment.\n- Loki log aggregation accessibility for MaaS component logs is confirmed or refuted, with the required label/filter scheme documented.\n- Perses dashboard deployment and live-data rendering against CKS Prometheus is confirmed or refuted.\n- OTel collector availability for MaaS trace export is confirmed or refuted.\n- If any element is not accessible, the provisioning delta (dedicated Prometheus/Loki stack for the MaaS namespace) is documented as additional scope.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (infrastructure feasibility portion, per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy).\n- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (infrastructure feasibility portion).\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- CKS provides Prometheus and Grafana Loki as standard infrastructure — \"Needs validation\" per the strategy; this investigation is the validation task.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65523,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"b1907aca-df55-45e1-9fec-98bd6c932a45","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:32:17.425Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
