{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-594ffe8f-04c9-4f40-8b9a-4a0d05d83f29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a77d0524b37b89e2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E004.md","content":"# MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS\n\n## Description\n\nPackage the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) as Helm charts for deployment on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS), replacing the OLM-based operator installation used on RHOAI. This is the foundational packaging work that enables all xKS deployment validation. CKS is the priority platform; the chart must also work on AKS.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Create Helm charts for the MaaS components from the existing kustomize-based deployment manifests (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md, deployment/base/), covering the maas-api Deployment/Service, maas-controller manager Deployment with CRDs and admission webhooks, and the payload-processing ext_proc server.\n- Expose configurable chart values for:\n  - GatewayClass name (xKS-native, e.g. `istio` on CKS — not `openshift-default`), with the MaaS HTTPRoute binding to a configurable Gateway.\n  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience) and group claim path mapping, sourced from the Tenant CRD configuration.\n  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager (replacing OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates).\n  - PostgreSQL connection (shared with other RHAII components or dedicated — a deployment-time configuration decision owned by the xKS Platform team).\n- Remove OpenShift-specific installation assumptions from the rendered manifests (OLM, OpenShift namespace conventions, OpenShift service-CA).\n- Provide chart values profiles for CKS (Istio GatewayClass with TLS/mTLS for Istio control-plane integration) and for AKS (validated GatewayClass options).\n- Stand up the Helm chart build/publish pipeline (the strategy's ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding prerequisite notes \"Helm chart build pipeline needed\").\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `helm install` of the MaaS chart on a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster renders all required resources (Deployments, Services, CRDs, webhooks, HTTPRoute, RBAC) without OpenShift-only resources failing.\n- GatewayClass name, OIDC issuer configuration, TLS certificate source, and PostgreSQL connection are all configurable via chart values, with documented defaults for CKS (Istio).\n- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager (not OpenShift service-CA) and cert-manager certificate rotation does not interrupt active requests (per strategy failure-mode criteria).\n- The Helm chart builds and publishes through the chart build pipeline (build pipeline green).\n- License scan of images and chart dependencies passes or exceptions are documented (strategy prerequisite: License Validation pending human review).\n- No changes to RHOAI MaaS GA installation paths — xKS packaging is additive (strategy NFR: backwards compatibility).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (priority platform per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — packaging portion.\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS — packaging portion.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Shared vs dedicated PostgreSQL for MaaS on xKS is an open configuration decision (xKS Platform) — handled as a chart value, not a blocker.\n- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is a pending human-review process gate.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66226,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"fe5f143a-3b42-4d7c-b4e0-7b3faf5f8579","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:32:31.032Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_d