{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1e57fdec-f1f5-416a-98ae-b46dbc2ce495","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a44414c389655b6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E006.md","content":"# maas-controller configurable OIDC group claim path mapping\n\n## Description\n\nMake the OIDC group claim path configurable in the maas-controller so that user group membership — which drives tier/subscription mapping and rate limiting — can be sourced from OIDC tokens with provider-varying claim formats (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) instead of Kubernetes RBAC groups. The MaaSSubscription controller maps rate limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`; this epic makes that claim path configurable per deployment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD (default: `auth.identity.groups`) — subject to the OIDC feasibility investigation confirming the CRD is not frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA.\n- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (architecture context: maas-controller/pkg/controller/maas/maassubscription_controller.go), so tier-to-group mapping uses the configured OIDC token claim.\n- Expose the group claim path as a Helm chart configuration value so it can be set per deployment without code changes.\n- Cover representative claim formats in tests: Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, and custom claim paths.\n- Ensure changes are additive/config-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior (Kubernetes RBAC group mapping) is unchanged when no custom claim path is set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n- Tier/subscription management (basic tier/subscription CRUD) functions with OIDC group claims, measured by successful subscription selection for an OIDC-authenticated user.\n- The default claim path (`auth.identity.groups`) preserves existing RHOAI behavior (backwards compatibility NFR).\n- Representative provider claim formats (Entra ID, Cognito, custom) are covered by automated tests.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the OIDC integration feasibility investigation on the MaaS 3.4 codebase: if the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA and no post-GA patch is possible, this epic is dropped and replaced by documenting the required claim format for customers (pushing IdP configuration burden to customer deployments), recorded as a known limitation.\n\n## Risks\n\n- OIDC group claim format variations across identity providers can break tier mapping — mitigated by the configurable claim path itself (strategy risk table).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67960,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"d010adb1-42d5-44b3-a971-0daa721616c6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:32:55.442Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
