{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-41f1dd50-9848-4465-b78c-8482a6e46578","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e542b9a5393c133","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E007.md","content":"# Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) deployment on CKS\n\n## Description\n\nDeploy and validate Kuadrant (Authorino for authentication, Limitador for token rate limiting) on CKS, the priority platform for RHAII MaaS on xKS. On RHOAI, RHCL deploys Kuadrant via OLM; on xKS (Helm-only), the deployment mechanism is selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation. The deliverable is working gateway-level authentication and rate limiting enforcement on CKS that the MaaS AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy resources integrate with.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Deploy Authorino + Limitador on a CKS cluster using the mechanism selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation, in priority order:\n  1. Primary: official RHCL Helm charts (if the OpenShift team commits xKS support).\n  2. Fallback: standalone Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm charts.\n  3. Contingency: direct Envoy ext_authz integration.\n- Validate the deployment against the Istio GatewayClass available on CKS (CoreWeave deploys with Istio service mesh), including TLS/mTLS configuration for Istio control-plane integration.\n- Validate that the Kuadrant CRs the MaaS controller generates (kuadrant.io/v1 AuthPolicy, kuadrant.io/v1alpha1 TokenRateLimitPolicy — architecture context: models-as-a-service.md) reconcile and enforce correctly on CKS under the selected mechanism.\n- Validate token rate limiting enforcement: Limitador returns HTTP 429 when a user exceeds the configured rate limit, and requests are denied with HTTP 503 when the Limitador pod is terminated (enforcement unavailable).\n- Document any CKS-specific constraints or deltas versus the OpenShift deployment.\n- Verify licensing of the deployed images and charts (strategy prerequisite: License Validation pending human review).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Authorino and Limitador are running and healthy on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n- Kuadrant AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy resources created by the MaaS controller reconcile successfully on CKS.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n- Given a MaaS deployment with the Limitador pod terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503 (rate limiting enforcement unavailable), measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n- The deployment mechanism, its fallback rationale, and any constraints are documented.\n- License validation of deployed images/charts passes or exceptions are documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — deployment portion.\n- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the RHCL xKS support investigation: if RHCL does not commit official xKS Helm charts, this epic is rewritten to the fallback (standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm) or contingency (direct Envoy ext_authz) mechanism, with escalation to product leadership per the strategy.\n\n## Risks\n\n- \"Kuadrant may not install on CKS\" (strategy risk table) — validated directly by this epic; fallback paths are in scope.\n- Lack of official RHCL support undermines long-term viability of MaaS on xKS (strategic dependency) — surfaced by the gating investigation, not resolved here.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68758,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"0d698428-7133-41f3-8f05-676a7705f6e7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:08.606Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
