{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-59b28aca-d6f2-4bcd-94fa-f6360e6f57a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf911fcdbc4e237f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E009.md","content":"# CKS observability integration (Prometheus, Loki, Perses)\n\n## Description\n\nIntegrate MaaS observability with the CKS platform infrastructure: wire the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape MaaS metrics, route MaaS structured logs into CKS Grafana Loki, and deploy the MaaS Perses dashboards against the CKS Prometheus instance. Owned by the xKS Platform team per the strategy's impacted-teams table (\"observability integration with CKS Prometheus/Loki\").\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape the MaaS metrics endpoints (dedicated metrics listener) from the MaaS namespace, per the scrape-target and network constraints confirmed by the CKS observability infrastructure validation.\n- Configure log shipping/aggregation so structured JSON logs from maas-api, Authorino, and Limitador are queryable in CKS Grafana Loki with the required label scheme.\n- Deploy the MaaS Perses dashboards (authored by the MaaS observability instrumentation work) against the CKS Prometheus instance.\n- If the CKS infrastructure validation found Prometheus/Loki not accessible for MaaS, provision a dedicated Prometheus and Loki stack for the MaaS namespace instead (gate remediation scope).\n- Validate the full observability data path against a deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- MaaS metrics endpoints are scraped by the CKS Prometheus instance (or the provisioned dedicated stack), and the MaaS metric series are queryable.\n- Structured logs from maas-api, Authorino, and Limitador are queryable in CKS Grafana Loki with label filters (timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, reason).\n- The MaaS Perses dashboard renders token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics with live data over the last 24 hours.\n- Any provisioning delta (dedicated Prometheus/Loki) is complete and documented if the shared CKS infrastructure was not accessible.\n- License scan of any provisioned observability images passes or exceptions are documented (strategy prerequisite: License Validation pending human review).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — CKS integration portion.\n- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection — CKS Loki aggregation portion.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the CKS observability infrastructure validation: if CKS Prometheus/Loki are not accessible for MaaS, this epic's scope grows to provisioning a dedicated stack before integration.\n- Consumes the metrics and dashboards produced by the maas-api observability instrumentation work, and is measured against a deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70532,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"829a64b0-3014-4d5a-9328-c50552c490a7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:32.244Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
