{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3a0227cd-6114-4c3d-b437-d0336584f9bb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94225c50bc84177a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-98wjqx0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E010.md","content":"# Structured logging for Authorino and Limitador\n\n## Description\n\nAdd structured JSON logging for authentication decisions in Authorino and rate limit enforcement in Limitador on xKS, so MaaS authentication and rate-limiting events are aggregatable in CKS Grafana Loki. Owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team per the strategy's affected-components table (\"structured logging for auth decisions\" / \"structured logging for rate limit enforcement\").\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable/extend structured JSON logging in Authorino covering authentication decisions: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason when denied.\n- Enable/extend structured logging in Limitador covering rate limit enforcement: 429 responses with exceeded quota identifiers (user, model, subscription as applicable).\n- Configure log output so entries are shipped to CKS Grafana Loki with the label scheme agreed with the CKS observability integration work.\n- Apply the logging configuration under the Kuadrant deployment mechanism selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation (official RHCL charts, standalone Helm, or direct Envoy ext_authz contingency — the last re-scopes this work to the corresponding auth components).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs in Authorino (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, and reason, measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n- Given a user exceeds a configured rate limit, the Limitador log entry records the enforcement event with the exceeded quota identifiers, measured by Loki queries.\n- Log volume and formatting do not impair the auth/rate-limiting data path (no synchronous blocking on log emission).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — Authorino/Limitador portion.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the RHCL xKS support investigation: the selected deployment mechanism determines where and how structured logging is configured for the auth and rate-limiting components; under the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency this epic is rewritten for the corresponding components.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Changes to RHCL-owned components require coordination with the OpenShift RHCL team; if official xKS support is not committed, changes may need to go upstream or be configuration-only.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71289,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fd07bf831150f8","agent_id":"a20fa1aa5b3a9ab51","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"01000fe7-9255-40b1-be8b-535a76a9f70c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:42.839Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003 into epics"}
