dency-gated):** E007, E010, E011, E012, E013, E015 — Kuadrant deployment on CKS, structured logging for RHCL components, full-stack CKS/AKS validation, tracing, and final documentation. Gated (directly or transitively) on E001.\n140\t\n141\tThe MaaS 3.4 GA stable-build timing (internal dependency, \"critical blocker\" for Summit) does not split tiers: no work can be validated without a build, and the strategy's mitigations (RC build by April 27, RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo) are timing tactics, not structural alternatives. Recorded as a health warning and an acceptance-criteria gate on the validation epics.\n142\t\n143\t## Health Warnings\n144\t\n145\t1. **Docs epic priority inversion (deliberate):** E015 is P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy `priority: Blocker` → P0) even though its underlying HLRs are P1 (known limitations) and P2 (identity flow). Flagged for human review of whether a P0 docs epic is intended for a Dev Preview.\n146\t2. **MaaS 3.4 GA build availability:** code freeze passed late March 2026; stable-build delivery timing is unknown and is a Summit-timeline risk. Not structurally modelable — recorded as an AC gate (use RC build; RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo) on E011/E012.\n147\t3. **Pending process gates:** Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding (Helm chart build pipeline), License Validation, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the strategy prerequisites. Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is an AC on E004; license verification of pulled images (Authorino, Limitador, Perses) is an AC on E007/E009; the rest are program-level gates outside Dev Preview scope per the strategy.\n148\t4. **Observability instrumentation freeze risk:** if maas-api is frozen at 3.4 GA, metrics instrumentation may need a post-3.4 patch or deferral of logging to P1 (strategy assumption \"Needs validation\"). Recorded as an assumption/AC on E008 rather than an Investigation — the epic exists either way; only landing timing changes.\n149\t5. **AKS GatewayClass choice** (`envoy-gateway` vs `azure-application-gateway`) is an implementation detail deferred to E012 — not a genuine unknown (either works; the strategy lists both as validated options).\n150\t6. **Shared vs dedicated PostgreSQL** for MaaS on xKS is a configuration decision (xKS Platform owns); captured as a configurable Helm value and AC on E004, not an Investigation.\n151\t\n152\t## Investigation Gate Summary\n153\t\n154\t| Investigation | Gated epics | Gate action | Fallback approach |\n155\t|---|---|---|---|\n156\t| E001 RHCL xKS support | E007, E010 | rewrite | If RHCL does not commit official xKS Helm charts: standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm deployment; contingency: direct Envoy ext_authz integration. Escalate to product leadership per strategy. |\n157\t| E002 OIDC feasibility on 3.4 codebase | E005 (rewrite), E006 (remove) | rewrite / remove | E006 fallback: if Tenant CRD is frozen, document the required OIDC group claim format and push IdP configuration burden to customers; record as a known limitation. |\n158\t| E003 CKS observability infrastructure | E009 | add_remediation | If CKS Prometheus/Loki are not accessible for MaaS, provision a dedicated Prometheus/Loki stack for the MaaS namespace before integration. |\n159\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867e2233e34bf131","agent_id":"a2fa96df2efbce081","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"cd52687a-fb18-46e5-8239-ca7c15bf3a0d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:47.672Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8332f15412a6e50d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
