{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a2923bfe0dbdd3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tPackage the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) as Helm charts for deployment on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS), replacing the OLM-based operator installation used on RHOAI. This is the foundational packaging work that enables all xKS deployment validation. CKS is the priority platform; the chart must also work on AKS.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Create Helm charts for the MaaS components from the existing kustomize-based deployment manifests (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md, deployment/base/), covering the maas-api Deployment/Service, maas-controller manager Deployment with CRDs and admission webhooks, and the payload-processing ext_proc server.\n38\t- Expose configurable chart values for:\n39\t  - GatewayClass name (xKS-native, e.g. `istio` on CKS — not `openshift-default`), with the MaaS HTTPRoute binding to a configurable Gateway.\n40\t  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience) and group claim path mapping, sourced from the Tenant CRD configuration.\n41\t  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager (replacing OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates).\n42\t  - PostgreSQL connection (shared with other RHAII components or dedicated — a deployment-time configuration decision owned by the xKS Platform team).\n43\t- Remove OpenShift-specific installation assumptions from the rendered manifests (OLM, OpenShift namespace conventions, OpenShift service-CA).\n44\t- Provide chart values profiles for CKS (Istio GatewayClass with TLS/mTLS for Istio control-plane integration) and for AKS (validated GatewayClass options).\n45\t- Stand up the Helm chart build/publish pipeline (the strategy's ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding prerequisite notes \"Helm chart build pipeline needed\").\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- `helm install` of the MaaS chart on a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster renders all required resources (Deployments, Services, CRDs, webhooks, HTTPRoute, RBAC) without OpenShift-only resources failing.\n50\t- GatewayClass name, OIDC issuer configuration, TLS certificate source, and PostgreSQL connection are all configurable via chart values, with documented defaults for CKS (Istio).\n51\t- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager (not OpenShift service-CA) and cert-manager certificate rotation does not interrupt active requests (per strategy failure-mode criteria).\n52\t- The Helm chart builds and publishes through the chart build pipeline (build pipeline green).\n53\t- License scan of images and chart dependencies passes or exceptions are documented (strategy prerequisite: License Validation pending human review).\n54\t- No changes to RHOAI MaaS GA installation paths — xKS packaging is additive (strategy NFR: backwards compatibility).\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (priority platform per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — packaging portion.\n59\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS — packaging portion.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks\n62\t\n63\t- Shared vs dedicated PostgreSQL for MaaS on xKS is an open configuration decision (xKS Platform) — handled as a chart value, not a blocker.\n64\t- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is a pending human-review process gate.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867e2233e34bf131","agent_id":"a2fa96df2efbce081","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"32c5ee16-7633-4e00-89f5-932b59bb7a34","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:55.415Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a2923bfe0dbdd3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
