{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b728ee17a9c450c6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E013\n3\ttitle: Distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E011\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tEnable distributed tracing through the full MaaS request path on xKS — gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend — using OpenTelemetry, per the Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy that observability is a core value proposition. P2 priority: deferrable beyond the Dev Preview core. maas-api already exports traces to an OpenTelemetry Collector via OTLP/gRPC (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md), so this extends existing foundations across the remaining hops.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Ensure W3C trace-context propagation across the request path: the gateway (Istio/Envoy on CKS), Authorino (ext_authz), Limitador (rate limiting), the payload-processing BBR ext_proc server, and the model backend.\n39\t- Configure trace export to an OpenTelemetry collector endpoint available on CKS (availability confirmed by the CKS observability infrastructure validation).\n40\t- Validate end-to-end traces for representative inference requests, including authenticated and rate-limited paths.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with tracing enabled, when an inference request traverses gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend, then a single correlated trace spans all hops, measured by querying the trace backend for a representative request.\n45\t- Trace propagation does not break authentication or rate limiting enforcement.\n46\t- Tracing overhead does not materially degrade request latency on the Dev Preview workload.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- [P2] Distributed tracing functional: gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy).\n51\t\n52\t## Assumptions\n53\t\n54\t- An OpenTelemetry collector is available or provisable on CKS (flagged in the CKS observability infrastructure validation).\n55\t- Tracing configuration for Authorino/Limitador depends on the Kuadrant deployment mechanism selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867e2233e34bf131","agent_id":"a2fa96df2efbce081","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"3a083bb4-cade-4bd9-8613-03ebfc5502e3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:39:16.942Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b728ee17a9c450c6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
