ant deployment mechanism outcome (including any fallback-path limitations).\n49\t- User identity flow for xKS deployments: customer-provided OIDC identity provider requirements (standards-compliant OIDC), how OIDC identity maps to MaaS subscriptions/tiers via group claims, and the API key flow.\n50\t- If triggered by the OIDC feasibility outcome: the required OIDC group claim format that customers must configure on their identity provider (fallback for the configurable group claim path).\n51\t- Content outline covering: deployment prerequisites (OIDC IdP, PostgreSQL, cert-manager, Gateway API implementation), authentication model, and Dev Preview scope exclusions (operator installation excluded — Helm only; Dashboard UI excluded).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A document exists listing all known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n56\t- The user identity flow for xKS deployments is documented: OIDC provider requirements, identity-to-subscription/tier mapping, and API key lifecycle.\n57\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implementation and validation outcomes (no unverified claims).\n58\t- Accuracy is validated against the architecture context (models-as-a-service.md) and the validated deployment behavior on CKS/AKS.\n59\t- If the group claim path fallback was triggered, the required customer IdP claim format is documented.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- [P1] Known limitations documented.\n64\t- [P2] User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n65\t\n66\t## Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Priority derives from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Blocker`) per the docs-authoring priority exception — it does not propagate to implementation epics.\n69\t- Documentation Support is a pending human-review process gate per the strategy prerequisites.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867e2233e34bf131","agent_id":"a2fa96df2efbce081","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"ac803b02-c82f-4762