ent. Logged as non-obvious mapping |\n23\t| Observability (Prometheus, Perses, Loki) | Model and Agent Observability | MaaS-specific observability work; closest canonical match |\n24\t| RHAII installation tooling (xKS Platform) | AI Core Platform | RHAII xKS deployment tooling is not in the component list; closest parent-level platform component. Logged as non-obvious mapping |\n25\t\n26\t**Component existence (architecture context):** `models-as-a-service.md` exists (in platform). Kuadrant/RHCL has no architecture-context file of its own (referenced within `models-as-a-service.md`, `PLATFORM.md`, `ai-gateway-operator.md`) — it is an external RHCL/OpenShift-owned dependency, which is why the RHCL xKS support question is modeled as a blocking Investigation rather than an onboarding chain. Gateway API on CKS is confirmed available (Istio on CoreWeave). CKS Prometheus/Loki is assumed but unvalidated — modeled as a blocking Investigation.\n27\t\n28\t## Epic List\n29\t\n30\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n31\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E001 | RHCL official xKS support status and deployment mechanism validation | Investigation | RHCL / OpenShift | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E002 | External OIDC integration feasibility on the MaaS 3.4 codebase | Investigation | MaaS | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E003 | CKS observability infrastructure accessibility validation | Investigation | xKS Platform | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E004 | MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E005 | maas-api external OIDC integration and OpenShift-assumption removal | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E006 | maas-controller configurable OIDC group claim path mapping | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E007 | Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) deployment on CKS | Implementation | RHCL / OpenShift | P0 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E008 | maas-api observability instrumentation and Perses dashboards | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E009 | CKS observability integration (Prometheus, Loki, Perses) | Implementation | xKS Platform | P0 |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E010 | Structured logging for Authorino and Limitador | Implementation | RHCL / OpenShift | P1 |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E011 | MaaS on CKS full-stack deployment validation | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E012 | MaaS on AKS deployment validation | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E013 | Distributed tracing through the MaaS request path | Implementation | MaaS | P2 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E014 | MaaS Helm chart integration with RHAII xKS installation tooling | Implementation | xKS Platform | P1 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8003-E015 | MaaS xKS documentation: known limitations and user identity flow | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n47\t\n48\tE015 priority note: `docs-authoring` priority exception applied — derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Blocker` (Blocker ≥ Critical → P0), not from its underlying P1/P2 HLRs, and it does not propagate upstream.\n49\t\n50\t## Dependency DAG\n51\t\n52\t```mermaid\n53\tgraph TD\n54\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8003-E001 RHCL xKS support Investigation]\n55\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8003-E002 OIDC feasibility Investigation]\n56\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8003-E003 CKS observability Investigation]\n57\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-8003-E004 Helm chart packaging]\n58\t    E008[RHAISTRAT-8003-E008 maas-api observability]\n59\t    E001 --> E007\n60\t    E001 --> E010\n61\t    E002 --> E005\n62\t    E002 --> E006\n63\t    E003 --> E009\n64\t    E004 --> E011\n65\t    E004 --> E014\n66\t    E005 --> E011\n67\t    E006 --> E011\n68\t    E007 --> E011\n69\t    E008 --> E009\n70\t    E009 --> E015\n71\t    E010 --> E015\n72\t    E011 --> E009\n73\t    E011 --> E012\n74\t    E011 --> E013\n75\t    E012 --> E015\n76\t    E013 --> E015\n77\t    E014 --> E015\n78\t    E004 --> E015\n79\t    E005 --> E015\n80\t    E006 --> E015\n81\t    E007 --> E015\n82\t    E008 --> E015\n83