{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7f199c5eb38b64a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E011\n3\ttitle: MaaS on CKS full-stack deployment validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: -1\n20\t  external_dependency: -1\n21\t  human_process_gates: -1\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\timplementation_type: null\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: Medium\n27\tai_implementability_score: 1\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# MaaS on CKS full-stack deployment validation\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tDeploy the full MaaS stack on CKS (the priority platform per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) via the Helm chart with external OIDC configuration, and validate core MaaS functionality: subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, external OIDC authentication, and API key authentication. Document what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta. This is the strategy's central Dev Preview deliverable: \"Validated MaaS deployment on at least one xKS platform\".\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Deploy MaaS on a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, via the Helm chart with OIDC configuration; verify maas-api and maas-controller pods run and are healthy.\n42\t- Validate core functionality against a customer-style OIDC provider:\n43\t  - OIDC JWT authentication for user identity.\n44\t  - API key creation, persistence in PostgreSQL, and use for model inference (`sk-oai-*` flow).\n45\t  - Subscription/tier management, including tier mapping driven by OIDC group claims.\n46\t  - Token rate limiting enforcement (HTTP 429 on exceeded limits).\n47\t- Validate failure modes per the strategy:\n48\t  - OIDC provider unavailable: API key requests continue; OIDC requests fail with HTTP 503 and descriptive error.\n49\t  - PostgreSQL unavailable: API key creation fails with HTTP 503; OIDC token authentication continues to succeed.\n50\t  - cert-manager TLS certificate rotation: active requests continue without interruption.\n51\t- Use the MaaS 3.4 RC/stable build per the timeline mitigation (RC by April 27 latest; RHOAI 3.3 MaaS fallback demo maintained if 3.4 integration fails).\n52\t- Record known limitations and the engineering delta (code changes, configuration changes, Helm chart packaging) discovered on CKS.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n57\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated API key.\n58\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n59\t- Given the OIDC provider becomes unavailable, inference requests using valid API keys continue to succeed while OIDC-authenticated requests fail with HTTP 503 and a descriptive error, measured by response status and error body.\n60\t- Given the PostgreSQL database becomes unavailable, API key creation requests fail with HTTP 503 while OIDC token-based authentication continues to succeed, measured by response status and error logs.\n61\t- Given cert-manager-issued TLS certificates are rotated, active inference requests continue without interruption and new requests succeed with the new certificate, measured by zero connection errors during the rotation window and successful TLS handshake validation post-rotation.\n62\t- What works, what breaks, and the engineering delta on CKS are documented (input to the known-limitations documentation).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (priority platform per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy).\n67\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS (end-to-end validation).\n68\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (end-to-end validation).\n69\t- [P0] API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS (end-to-end validation).\n70\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (end-to-end validation).\n71\t\n72\t## Risks\n73\t\n74\t- MaaS 3.4 GA build availability is a timing risk (code freeze late March 2026; stable build timing unknown) — mitigated per the strategy: RC build by April 27, parallel CKS validation, RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo.\n75\t- PostgreSQL unavailability during validation — mitigated by the in-memory LRU cache (TTL 5 min) for validated API key hashes per the strategy risk table, if implemented.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dc1998c3ea04559","agent_id":"ad6f88bf8523a0ee8","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"f013e37f-0628-4b7c-9edc-4ea0cc587fd4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:48:15.374Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7f199c5eb38b64a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
