{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9773dfdbcac439c9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: External OIDC integration feasibility on the MaaS 3.4 codebase\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# External OIDC integration feasibility on the MaaS 3.4 codebase\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the open questions around external OIDC authentication on the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase before implementation begins: whether the existing MaaS AuthPolicy can leverage external OIDC as-is or requires changes, and whether the configurable OIDC group claim path mapping can be implemented without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes (i.e., whether the Tenant CRD is frozen). The answers determine the scope of the maas-api and maas-controller OIDC implementation work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Validate against the models-as-a-service codebase (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md) that the existing AuthPolicy generation (MaaSAuthPolicy reconciler constructs Kuadrant AuthPolicy with API key, TokenReview, and optional OIDC JWT methods) can be configured to use Authorino's `oidc` identity source with a customer-provided issuer URL and JWKS endpoint, and identify exactly what changes (if any) are needed.\n34\t- Confirm the Tenant CRD's existing external OIDC configuration fields (`oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`, `oidcAudience`) are sufficient for basic OIDC integration on xKS.\n35\t- Determine whether a `groupClaimPath` field can be added to the Tenant CRD and passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation given the MaaS 3.4 GA code freeze (late March 2026) — i.e., is the CRD frozen, and is a post-GA patch acceptable to release management?\n36\t- Validate the assumed OIDC group claim formats across representative identity providers (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) against the CEL predicate evaluation path (`auth.identity.groups`).\n37\t- Confirm the API key authentication flow (`sk-oai-*` via the maas-api callback validation endpoint) is genuinely OIDC-agnostic and requires no changes.\n38\t- Deliverable: a feasibility decision record covering (a) AuthPolicy OIDC reuse verdict with the exact change delta, and (b) groupClaimPath feasibility verdict (code change possible vs Tenant CRD frozen).\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- A concrete verdict on AuthPolicy external-OIDC reuse: configuration-only, or an enumerated list of required code changes in the MaaS components.\n43\t- A concrete verdict on group claim path configurability: either the Tenant CRD change is feasible (with the freeze-policy confirmation from release management), or the fallback is confirmed necessary (document required claim format, push IdP configuration burden to customers).\n44\t- The API key flow's OIDC independence is verified against the codebase with cited evidence.\n45\t- Representative OIDC provider group claim formats are documented against the CEL predicate path.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (feasibility portion).\n50\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) — feasibility portion.\n51\t\n52\t## Open Questions Resolved by this Investigation\n53\t\n54\t- \"Can we leverage existing MaaS AuthPolicy with external OIDC, or are changes needed?\"\n55\t- \"How do we map external identities to MaaS subscriptions/tiers?\" (claim path feasibility portion)\n56\t- Assumption: \"OIDC group claim path can be made configurable without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes — Needs validation.\"\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6290c29df86f11f","agent_id":"a91fef4195d5ac548","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"26e0b8ff-797e-4916-bb02-5b8f968e9007","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:56:09.448Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9773dfdbcac439c9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
