{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c9a119b7263ee86","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: maas-controller configurable OIDC group claim path mapping\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA and no post-GA patch\n15\t    is possible, drop the code change and instead document the required OIDC group\n16\t    claim format, pushing IdP configuration burden to customer deployments; record\n17\t    as a known limitation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# maas-controller configurable OIDC group claim path mapping\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake the OIDC group claim path configurable in the maas-controller so that user group membership — which drives tier/subscription mapping and rate limiting — can be sourced from OIDC tokens with provider-varying claim formats (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) instead of Kubernetes RBAC groups. The MaaSSubscription controller maps rate limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`; this epic makes that claim path configurable per deployment.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Add a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD (default: `auth.identity.groups`) — subject to the OIDC feasibility investigation confirming the CRD is not frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA.\n44\t- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (architecture context: maas-controller/pkg/controller/maas/maassubscription_controller.go), so tier-to-group mapping uses the configured OIDC token claim.\n45\t- Expose the group claim path as a Helm chart configuration value so it can be set per deployment without code changes.\n46\t- Cover representative claim formats in tests: Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, and custom claim paths.\n47\t- Ensure changes are additive/config-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior (Kubernetes RBAC group mapping) is unchanged when no custom claim path is set.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n52\t- Tier/subscription management (basic tier/subscription CRUD) functions with OIDC group claims, measured by successful subscription selection for an OIDC-authenticated user.\n53\t- The default claim path (`auth.identity.groups`) preserves existing RHOAI behavior (backwards compatibility NFR).\n54\t- Representative provider claim formats (Entra ID, Cognito, custom) are covered by automated tests.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n59\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n60\t\n61\t## Dependencies and Gating\n62\t\n63\t- Gated by the OIDC integration feasibility investigation on the MaaS 3.4 codebase: if the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA and no post-GA patch is possible, this epic is dropped and replaced by documenting the required claim format for customers (pushing IdP configuration burden to customer deployments), recorded as a known limitation.\n64\t\n65\t## Risks\n66\t\n67\t- OIDC group claim format variations across identity providers can break tier mapping — mitigated by the configurable claim path itself (strategy risk table).\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6290c29df86f11f","agent_id":"a91fef4195d5ac548","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"94eb188e-83c2-44dd-b376-7ac5551fc616","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:56:13.873Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c9a119b7263ee86","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
