{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8bb61412edca60a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n3\ttitle: Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) deployment on CKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: 'If RHCL does not commit official xKS Helm charts, rewrite to\n15\t    the fallback mechanism: standalone Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm charts;\n16\t    if that fails on CKS, use direct Envoy ext_authz integration as contingency, escalating\n17\t    to product leadership per the strategy.'\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) deployment on CKS\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDeploy and validate Kuadrant (Authorino for authentication, Limitador for token rate limiting) on CKS, the priority platform for RHAII MaaS on xKS. On RHOAI, RHCL deploys Kuadrant via OLM; on xKS (Helm-only), the deployment mechanism is selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation. The deliverable is working gateway-level authentication and rate limiting enforcement on CKS that the MaaS AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy resources integrate with.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Deploy Authorino + Limitador on a CKS cluster using the mechanism selected by the RHCL xKS support investigation, in priority order:\n44\t  1. Primary: official RHCL Helm charts (if the OpenShift team commits xKS support).\n45\t  2. Fallback: standalone Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm charts.\n46\t  3. Contingency: direct Envoy ext_authz integration.\n47\t- Validate the deployment against the Istio GatewayClass available on CKS (CoreWeave deploys with Istio service mesh), including TLS/mTLS configuration for Istio control-plane integration.\n48\t- Validate that the Kuadrant CRs the MaaS controller generates (kuadrant.io/v1 AuthPolicy, kuadrant.io/v1alpha1 TokenRateLimitPolicy — architecture context: models-as-a-service.md) reconcile and enforce correctly on CKS under the selected mechanism.\n49\t- Validate token rate limiting enforcement: Limitador returns HTTP 429 when a user exceeds the configured rate limit, and requests are denied with HTTP 503 when the Limitador pod is terminated (enforcement unavailable).\n50\t- Document any CKS-specific constraints or deltas versus the OpenShift deployment.\n51\t- Verify licensing of the deployed images and charts (strategy prerequisite: License Validation pending human review).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Authorino and Limitador are running and healthy on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass.\n56\t- Kuadrant AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy resources created by the MaaS controller reconcile successfully on CKS.\n57\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n58\t- Given a MaaS deployment with the Limitador pod terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503 (rate limiting enforcement unavailable), measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n59\t- The deployment mechanism, its fallback rationale, and any constraints are documented.\n60\t- License validation of deployed images/charts passes or exceptions are documented.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- [P0] RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input guidance embedded in the strategy) — deployment portion.\n65\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS.\n66\t\n67\t## Dependencies and Gating\n68\t\n69\t- Gated by the RHCL xKS support investigation: if RHCL does not commit official xKS Helm charts, this epic is rewritten to the fallback (standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm) or contingency (direct Envoy ext_authz) mechanism, with escalation to product leadership per the strategy.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks\n72\t\n73\t- \"Kuadrant may not install on CKS\" (strategy risk table) — validated directly by this epic; fallback paths are in scope.\n74\t- Lack of official RHCL support undermines long-term viability of MaaS on xKS (strategic dependency) — surfaced by the gating investigation, not resolved here.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6290c29df86f11f","agent_id":"a91fef4195d5ac548","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"5db755e4-956b-4dce-b43f-defe4f74a39e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:56:14.905Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8bb61412edca60a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
