{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84567911ca4aa8b0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E012\n3\ttitle: MaaS on AKS deployment validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E011\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# MaaS on AKS deployment validation\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tValidate the MaaS xKS Dev Preview deployment on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), satisfying the RFE acceptance criterion of \"AKS AND CKS\". Runs after the CKS validation (priority platform) and reuses the validated Helm chart, OIDC configuration, and Kuadrant deployment mechanism, adapting the GatewayClass to an AKS-native option.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Deploy MaaS on an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and a Gateway API implementation installed, via the Helm chart with OIDC configuration; verify maas-api and maas-controller pods run and are healthy.\n39\t- Select and configure the AKS GatewayClass from the strategy's validated options (`envoy-gateway` multi-platform, or `azure-application-gateway`) — an implementation decision for this epic.\n40\t- Re-run the core functional validation performed on CKS: OIDC authentication, API key lifecycle, subscription/tier management with OIDC group claims, token rate limiting (HTTP 429), and the failure modes (OIDC outage, PostgreSQL unavailability, TLS rotation).\n41\t- Document AKS-specific deltas, constraints, and known limitations versus CKS and versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n46\t- Core functionality validated on AKS: OIDC JWT authentication, API key creation and inference use, subscription/tier management with group claims, and rate limiting returning HTTP 429 on exceeded limits.\n47\t- Failure modes validated on AKS: API key requests survive OIDC provider unavailability; API key creation fails gracefully (HTTP 503) on PostgreSQL unavailability while OIDC authentication continues; cert-manager TLS rotation does not interrupt requests.\n48\t- AKS-specific known limitations and engineering deltas are documented (input to the known-limitations documentation).\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (RFE acceptance criterion: \"AKS AND CKS\").\n53\t\n54\t## Assumptions\n55\t\n56\t- Learnings, Helm chart, OIDC configuration, and the Kuadrant deployment mechanism from the CKS validation transfer to AKS with GatewayClass adaptation only.\n57\t- AKS provides (or the deployment provisions) an equivalent of the CKS observability infrastructure; observability validation on AKS is not separately required by the strategy's acceptance criteria, which name CKS.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6290c29df86f11f","agent_id":"a91fef4195d5ac548","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a7a","uuid":"bd57df7d-e6a8-4385-83c2-def54e375f0d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:56:23.524Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84567911ca4aa8b0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
