{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac669df8375c744e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E014\n3\ttitle: MaaS Helm chart integration with RHAII xKS installation tooling\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 0\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Low\n24\tai_implementability_score: -1\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# MaaS Helm chart integration with RHAII xKS installation tooling\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tIntegrate the MaaS Helm chart into the RHAII xKS deployment strategy and installation tooling, so MaaS can be installed as part of a full RHAII deployment on xKS rather than only standalone. Owned by the xKS Platform team per the strategy's impacted-teams table (\"Helm chart integration with RHAII xKS deployment strategy\"). Primarily enables the RHAII Tech Preview path (Summit May 2026 timeline); the Dev Preview validations deploy the chart directly.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Incorporate the MaaS Helm chart into the RHAII xKS installation tooling as a deployable component, including prerequisite ordering (Kuadrant, Gateway API implementation, PostgreSQL, cert-manager). The Kuadrant prerequisite is encoded as a configurable prerequisite covering the bounded fallback ladder from the RHCL xKS support investigation (official RHCL Kuadrant charts, standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm deployment, or the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency) rather than hard-coding whichever mechanism that investigation selects — the deliverable (prerequisites ordered and installed before MaaS) is identical under every outcome, so the tooling does not depend on the mechanism-selection outcome.\n39\t- Define the MaaS configuration surface within the RHAII xKS deployment values (OIDC issuer configuration, gateway class, PostgreSQL connection — shared or dedicated per the xKS Platform decision).\n40\t- Document the installation path and prerequisites for platform teams deploying RHAII with MaaS capabilities on xKS.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A RHAII xKS deployment that includes MaaS installs the MaaS Helm chart with its prerequisites in a single tooling-driven flow.\n45\t- MaaS configuration (OIDC, gateway class, PostgreSQL) is expressed through the RHAII xKS deployment values without chart modification.\n46\t- The integrated installation is demonstrated on at least one xKS platform.\n47\t- The installation path and prerequisites are documented.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- Supports [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS and on AKS — packaging/installation integration for the RHAII Tech Preview path (no standalone HLR; the deployment HLRs are validated by the CKS/AKS validation epics).\n52\t\n53\t## Assumptions\n54\t\n55\t- The RHAII xKS deployment strategy and tooling (related strategy RHAISTRAT-7177 outcome path) accept additional Helm-based components.\n56\t- Dev Preview validation does not depend on this integration (charts deploy standalone); this epic targets the Tech Preview packaging path.\n57\t- The Kuadrant deployment mechanism is not a dependency: the prerequisite ordering encodes the investigation's bounded fallback ladder as configurable prerequisites (see Scope), so no edge to the RHCL xKS support investigation or the Kuadrant deployment epic is needed.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6290c29df86f11f","agent_id":"a91fef4195d5ac548","session_id":"b158df32-2239-4f0e-abf0-6598f1f60a